{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966816,"nonce":"7pfr9S4RZqUr7huQD858ZTA2ozE=","title":"blinc_cn → blinc_layout widget promotion plan","message":"Promote a set of fundamental interaction primitives from `blinc_cn::components` to `blinc_layout::widgets`. Each promotion is a **rewrite with CSS awareness**, not a file move — the goal is first-class blinc_layout primitives that third-party theme crates can build on without depending on `blinc_cn`'s shadcn styling.\n\n**Why:**\n1. The current `blinc_cn` components (popover, dialog, collapsible, tabs, tree, slider, switch, tooltip, select, combobox, menus — 500-1000+ lines each) contain real interaction primitives trapped inside shadcn-styled wrappers. A third-party material-themed or iOS-themed widget crate cannot reuse them without pulling in blinc_cn as a dep.\n2. The `html_view()` widget plan (see `project_html_view_plan.md`) benefits directly — its DOM walker targets `blinc_layout` primitives, so promotion means more tags get free coverage with cleaner semantics.\n3. Promoted primitives can be properly CSS-overridable via Blinc's existing `Stylesheet` + `apply_stylesheet_*` pipeline, which is currently inconsistent across cn components (several have known bugs — see quality audit below).\n4. The architectural principle matches the existing pattern: `blinc_layout::widgets::button` is the behavior primitive; `blinc_cn::button` is the styled shadcn variant over it. Checkbox, radio, and text_area already follow this split. The promoted components adopt the same shape.\n\n**How to apply:** Work through the priority-ordered candidate list below. For each candidate, do the full rewrite checklist (not a file copy). When scoping widget or html_view work, check whether the referenced widget is already promoted — unpromoted primitives should not be built on from `blinc_layout` internals, and promoted ones should not retain their old `blinc_cn` behavior copy.\n\n---\n\n\nA component belongs in `blinc_layout` if ALL of these hold:\n\n1. **Fundamental interaction pattern** — disclosure, selection, dismissal, floating anchor, form control. Not \"styled visual\".\n2. **Multiple design systems would want to build on it** — shadcn, material, fluent, iOS-ish, terminal, etc.\n3. **Non-trivial enough to not be a composition** — has a state machine, keyboard nav, focus management, or event routing that would be wasteful to re-implement.\n4. **Can't be cleanly built from existing primitives + CSS alone** — if `blinc_cn::foo` is just `Div` + `.class(...)` + existing primitive, it stays in cn.\n\nA component stays in `blinc_cn` if any of these hold:\n\n1. It's a composition of existing primitives with a design opinion (card, sidebar, breadcrumb).\n2. It's a styling wrapper over a primitive (`cn::button` over `layout::button`).\n3. It's a layout helper (`aspect_ratio`).\n4. It's a loading placeholder (`spinner`, `skeleton`).\n\n---\n\n\nEvery promotion must satisfy ALL of these, not just \"file moved\":\n\n- [ ] Widget exposes a stable default class (e.g. `blinc-popover`, `blinc-dialog`, `blinc-tabs`) that user stylesheets can target.\n- [ ] `element_classes()` is forwarded correctly in any custom `impl ElementBuilder` block. **Known gotcha**: the default trait method returns `\u0026[]`, so without the override, `.class(...)` is invisible to the renderer's class-based selector matching. This has bit the existing blinc_cn components at least once — audit every candidate for it during promotion.\n- [ ] Namespace convention: `blinc-{widget}` for the base class, `blinc-{widget}--{variant}` for variants, `blinc-{widget}--{state}` for states. Do NOT use `#id`-style selectors (they'd conflict with user-land ids).\n\n- [ ] `:hover`, `:focus`, `:active`, `:disabled` work out of the box for interactive primitives.\n- [ ] Selection/toggle primitives support `:checked` via `ElementState::Checked` (see checkbox / radio for the reference pattern).\n- [ ] State styles go through `apply_stylesheet_state_styles()` — do NOT hardcode hover/focus visuals in the primitive.\n\n- [ ] Primitive does NOT hardcode `padding`, `gap`, `margin`, `width`, `height` for properties that authors will want to override.\n- [ ] `apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides()` picks up `.blinc-{widget}` rules and modifies taffy styles before `compute_layout()`. Verify this works end-to-end with an example stylesheet during promotion.\n- [ ] `base_taffy_styles` snapshot is captured so layout animations and state transitions can reset cleanly.\n\n- [ ] `apply_element_style_to_props()` picks up visual CSS and modifies `RenderProps`. Verify with an example that overrides background, border, corner-radius, opacity.\n- [ ] `base_styles` snapshot is captured so visual animations and state transitions can reset cleanly.\n- [ ] **CSS vs inline conflict**: the primitive should NOT set visual props inline for any property that authors are expected to control via CSS. If a prop is in `cn_styles.rs` or in the promoted default stylesheet, don't also hardcode it on the builder.\n\n- [ ] Animatable properties (opacity, transform, color, corner_radius, padding/margin/gap, background, border) work under `@keyframes` and `transition:` declarations.\n- [ ] `css_animations` and `css_transitions` HashMaps are populated correctly for the widget's nodes.\n- [ ] For widgets with built-in animated transitions (collapsible expand, dialog fade-in, tab content swap), verify CSS transitions override the built-in animations cleanly — authors should be able to replace the default motion.\n- [ ] Remember: CSS animation ticking is synchronous on the main thread, not the AnimationScheduler background thread. The `css_animating` flag → `request_redraw()` chain drives redraws.\n\n- [ ] Tab order works (the primitive participates in focus traversal).\n- [ ] Primitive-specific keys work: arrow keys in menus/tabs/slider, escape in dialog/popover, space/enter for activation, home/end for list traversal.\n- [ ] Focus trap for modal dialogs. Focus return for popover/dialog on dismiss.\n- [ ] A minimal `aria_role` + `aria_label` API surface on the builder for downstream a11y layers.\n\n- [ ] Read the current `blinc_cn` version's issue history (git log, test failures, known gotchas) and fix anything that surfaces during the rewrite.\n- [ ] Specific suspects to check: `element_classes()` forwarding; state transitions reverse on hover-leave (see the `prev_affected` pattern in the renderer); CSS animation restart loops from completed-transition pruning; cursor positioning during text input within floating widgets.\n- [ ] Write at least one regression test per known bug you fix, targeting the primitive level (not the blinc_cn wrapper).\n\n- [ ] After the primitive lands in `blinc_layout`, the existing `blinc_cn::\u003ccomponent\u003e` becomes a thin wrapper that: adds the shadcn class names, applies shadcn defaults via `cn_styles.rs`, and re-exports the primitive's builder API.\n- [ ] Delete the duplicated interaction logic from the cn version — it should be \u003c100 lines after promotion.\n- [ ] Verify every existing blinc_cn usage and example still works after the rewrite.\n\n- [ ] Add to the blinc_layout widget README/doc comment section.\n- [ ] Ship an example in `crates/blinc_app/examples/` that exercises the primitive directly (not via blinc_cn) and demonstrates CSS override.\n- [ ] Update `project_html_view_plan.md`'s tag→widget inventory if the promotion changes which crate the walker maps a tag to.\n\n---\n\n\nDependency chain matters — `popover` unblocks six downstream promotions. Do it first.\n\n\n| Priority | Candidate | Current size | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **popover** | 604 lines | Foundational floating-anchor primitive. Everything that floats depends on it: tooltip, hover_card, dropdown_menu, context_menu, menubar, navigation_menu, select, combobox, date pickers. Ship first. |\n| 2 | **dialog** | 600 lines | `\u003cdialog\u003e` HTML semantic. Modal overlay, backdrop, focus trap, escape, return value. Already has `blinc_layout::widgets::overlay` as the lower-level manager. |\n| 3 | **collapsible** | 558 lines | `\u003cdetails\u003e`/`\u003csummary\u003e` HTML semantic. Disclosure with animated height. Used by accordion, sidebar, tree, menus. |\n| 4 | **tabs** | 999 lines | Keyboard-navigable panel switcher. Core UI pattern. Tabs are used standalone constantly. |\n| 5 | **slider** | 774 lines | `\u003cinput type=\"range\"\u003e` HTML form control. Should be a peer of `layout::checkbox` / `layout::radio`. |\n| 6 | **switch** | 516 lines | Fundamental toggle, semantically distinct from checkbox (binary state vs. selection). |\n| 7 | **tree** | 694 lines | Hierarchical expand/collapse with keyboard nav + selection. File browsers, docs outlines. |\n\n\nThese are thin once popover lands. Do them after Wave 1 entry 1.\n\n| Priority | Candidate | Current size | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | **tooltip** | 589 lines | Hover/focus-revealed label over popover. Possibly merge into popover as a `hover_card()` variant to avoid duplication. |\n| 9 | **select** | 706 lines | `\u003cselect\u003e`/`\u003coption\u003e` HTML form control: popover + list + keyboard nav. |\n| 10 | **combobox** | 950 lines | `\u003cinput list\u003e`/`\u003cdatalist\u003e` with filtering: popover + text_edit + list. |\n\n\n| Priority | Candidate | Current total | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 11 | **menu** (new primitive) | ~3200 lines (4 files) | Unify `context_menu` (1036) + `dropdown_menu` (1166) + `menubar` + `navigation_menu` into one `blinc_layout::widgets::menu` primitive that takes a trigger type (click, right-click, hover, focus) as configuration. The four cn versions become thin wrappers that set the trigger. This is the biggest lift but the highest architectural payoff — 90% of the code across those files is shared. |\n\n\n`accordion` (composition), `alert`, `aspect_ratio`, `avatar`, `badge`, `breadcrumb`, `button` (already promoted via layout::button), `card`, `chart`, `checkbox` (already), `drawer`, `sheet`, `sidebar` (all dialog variants with slide direction), `hover_card` (popover variant — consider merging into popover primitive), `icon`, `input` (styles `text_edit`), `kbd`, `label`, `pagination`, `progress`, `radio` (already), `resizable` (borderline — small enough to stay in cn), `scroll_area` (styles `layout::scroll`), `separator` (styles `layout::hr`), `skeleton`, `spinner`, `textarea` (already styles `text_area`), `toast`, `typography`.\n\n---\n\n\nPer candidate: **~3-5 days** (rewrite primitive + CSS pipeline wiring + bug audit + regression tests + shim the blinc_cn wrapper + example + doc comment). This is significantly more than the \"1-2 days to move a file\" I originally suggested — the per-candidate checklist above has nine sections, and the CSS-awareness work alone (sections 3, 4, 5) is typically 1-2 days per component.\n\nTotal for all 11 waves: **~6-8 weeks** of focused work. The `menu` consolidation (Wave 3) is the biggest single item at ~1.5-2 weeks on its own because it touches four existing components.\n\n\nWidget promotion can run independently of `html_view()` Phase 1 — the walker can target the existing `blinc_cn` versions for now and be updated later when each promotion lands. However, if the two plans overlap in time, coordinate so the walker's tag→widget mapping doesn't need to be rewritten twice. Recommended sequencing:\n\n1. Widget promotion Wave 1 (popover, dialog, collapsible, tabs, slider, switch, tree)\n2. html_view `project_html_view_plan.md` Phase 1 walker + Phase 0 missing widgets (can parallelize with tail of Wave 1)\n3. Widget promotion Wave 2 (tooltip, select, combobox)\n4. html_view Phases 2-4\n5. Widget promotion Wave 3 (menu consolidation) — do last because it's the biggest and html_view isn't blocked on it\n\n\n- **Breaking the `blinc_cn` public API.** Every promotion must keep the existing `blinc_cn::component()` call shape working — users who depend on the shadcn-styled versions should not need to change a single line.\n- **Promoting styling opinions.** The promotion is strictly about interaction primitives. Color tokens, spacing scales, border-radius defaults stay in `blinc_cn::cn_styles` or whatever theme crate is in use. The promoted primitive defaults to \"blank\" visuals that CSS must style.\n- **Deleting `blinc_cn` components.** They become thin wrappers, not deletions.\n- **Adding new primitives that don't currently exist.** This plan is about rehoming existing behavior, not building new widgets. New primitives go through the normal widget-building process.\n\n\n- **Known gotcha reference**: audit `element_classes()` forwarding in EVERY cn component during promotion, not just the candidates. This bug has surfaced before and is easy to introduce.\n- **CSS integration reference**: when in doubt about how a primitive should integrate with the stylesheet pipeline, read `blinc_layout::widgets::button` and `blinc_layout::widgets::checkbox` — they're the reference implementations for \"primitive with state, CSS overrides, and a blinc_cn styled wrapper on top\". Match their shape.\n- **Bug discovery via tests**: the promotion process will surface bugs that weren't previously visible because the cn versions had never been exercised under the full `apply_stylesheet_*` pipeline. Every bug found during promotion gets a regression test at the primitive level.\n- **Success metric**: after all waves, a third-party material-themed or iOS-themed widget crate should be buildable as a pure consumer of `blinc_layout::widgets::*` with zero `blinc_cn` dependency. Ship a skeleton `crates/blinc_mt/` (material-themed) example after Wave 2 to prove this works.","files":null}]}